  "bodyTypst": "#image(\"/imgs/ap-calc-bc-2016-frq-02-diagram-01.jpg\", width: 65%)\n\nAt time $t$, the position of a particle moving in the $x y$-plane is given by the parametric functions $(x(t)\\, y(t))$, where $frac(d x,d t)= t^(2)+ sin lr((3 t^(2)))$. The graph of $y$, consisting of three line segments, is shown in the figure above. At $t = 0$, the particle is at position $(5 \\,1)$.\n\n(a) Find the position of the particle at $t = 3$.\n\n(b) Find the slope of the line tangent to the path of the particle at $t = 3$.\n\n(c) Find the speed of the particle at $t = 3$.\n\n(d) Find the total distance traveled by the particle from $t = 0$ to $t = 2$.",
